---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/seo';

const title = 'Privacy: your files never leave your browser';
const description = 'How Vexyn handles your data: it does not. Every tool runs in your browser and your file is never uploaded.';
const schema = breadcrumbSchema([
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy', url: '/privacy' },
]);
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} schema={schema}>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-6">Privacy</h1>

    <div class="space-y-5 text-[color:var(--color-text-mute)] leading-relaxed">
      <p>Short version: your files and their contents never leave your browser.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[color:var(--color-text)] mt-8 mb-2">Your data</h2>
      <p>
        When you use a Vexyn tool, the file you drop in is read and processed entirely by JavaScript running in your browser. It is never uploaded to a server. We could not see it if we wanted to — there is no upload endpoint. You can verify this yourself: open your browser's developer tools, go to the Network tab, and use any tool. No request carries your data out.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[color:var(--color-text)] mt-8 mb-2">What we do collect</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing that identifies you. We do not require an account and we set no cookies. For basic traffic counts we run our own first-party, cookieless analytics: each pageview records the page, a coarse country and device type, and a per-day rotating hash (of IP and browser) used only to estimate unique visitors — it cannot be tied back to you and is never stored as a profile. No third-party analytics, no cross-site tracking, no advertising IDs on our side.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[color:var(--color-text)] mt-8 mb-2">Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        The tools are funded by display advertising. Ad networks may set their own cookies to serve and measure ads. This is standard for ad-supported sites; it never has access to the files you process, because those never leave your browser in the first place.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[color:var(--color-text)] mt-8 mb-2">Browser storage</h2>
      <p>
        Some tools remember small preferences (like your theme) in your browser's local storage. One tool can store more: the Net Worth Analyzer will keep the accounts you type in, but only if you tick the box asking it to — it is off by default, the data is held unencrypted in that one browser, and a "Clear saved data" button removes it. Everything stored this way stays on your device and is never sent anywhere.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
